| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Recommendation |
|---|----------|-------|----------|----------------|
| 1 | 🟡 Medium | **No rate limiting** | `app.get(...)` routes | Add `express-rate-limit` to prevent DoS/brute-force. |
| 2 | 🟡 Medium | **No authentication/authorization** | `/users` route | The `/users` endpoint returns PII (names + emails) with zero auth. Add JWT, session, or API key middleware. |
| 3 | 🟡 Medium | **No security headers** | App-level middleware | Add `helmet` to set secure HTTP headers (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, etc.). |
| 4 | 🟠 Low-Med | **No input validation middleware** | App-level | Add `express-validator` or similar — important for any future routes that accept input. |
| 5 | 🟢 Low | **No CORS policy** | App-level | Without explicit CORS config, cross-origin behavior depends on defaults. Use the `cors` package to define an explicit allowlist. |
| 6 | 🟢 Low | **Hardcoded port** | `app.listen(3000)` | Use `process.env.PORT \|\| 3000` to support environment-based configuration. |
| 7 | 🟢 Low | **No error handling middleware** | App-level | Add a global error handler `(err, req, res, next)` to avoid leaking stack traces. |
| 8 | 🟢 Low | **No request body parser with size limit** | App-level | If POST routes are added, always set a body size limit: `express.json({ limit: '10kb' })`. |

